    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128-a1">

                <pb facs="0189" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg129"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 2343.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to the
                            Tsung-li Yamên</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-06"><hi rendition="#small-caps">September</hi> 6,
                            1895</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 27.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Highnesses and Your Excellencies</hi>: I have
                    the honor to inform you that I have been ordered by my Government to organize
                    immediately a commission, consisting of Mr. Sheridan P. Read, United States
                    consul at Tientsin, a naval officer of the United States, and an American
                    missionary, to proceed to Chengtu and there investigate the pauses and other
                    masters connoted with the recent antiforeign riots in <pb facs="0190" n="130"
                        xml:id="pg130"/> the province of Szechuan. I am also directed to ask your
                    highnesses and your excellencies to appoint an official of suitable rank to
                    accompany this commission and sit as a member thereof. It is my opinion that it
                    is desirable that an official be sent from Peking. I am also directed to request
                    you to furnish for this commission an ample escort and to direct the officials
                    in Szechuan to afford it every facility for the discharge of its important
                    duties.</p>
                <p>I should be much pleased to have an early and full answer to the matters herein
                    stated.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
